{title: Beatitudes}
{artist: Bethel Music}
{key: A}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Verse 1}
[A]Blessed are the poorest ones
For heaven come to where they are
in [E]You, in [B]You
[A]Blessed are the ones who mourn
For comfort comes to find them all
in [E]You, in [B]You

{comment: Chorus}
So [A]blessed are the [E]ones who [B]call Your name
and [A]blessed are the [E]ones You s[B]ave
for [A]You bless the [E]pure in [B]heart
and we will see our G[A]od
yes we will see our G[B]od

{comment: Verse 2}
Th[A]ose who seek will be made right
They will be filled and lifted high
in Y[E]ou, in Y[B]ou
B[A]lessed are the merciful
For mercy will be shown to them
by Y[E]ou, by Y[B]ou

{comment: Bridge}
If just to kn[A]ow You, if just to lo[B]ve You
What more can I a[C#m]sk for?
What more can [E/G#]I ask for?
